# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# The path rules of Koinon's CI and local gates: ONE source. Read by hack/paths-lib.sh and, through
# it, by hack/ci-changes.sh (which CI jobs a change turns on), hack/needs-e2e.sh (the kind e2e),
# hack/preflight.sh (which local gates run) and hack/lane-gates.sh (which local gate stands for a CI
# job). No script keeps a private copy of a pattern. Why each rule exists: docs/dev/ci.md#path-rules.
#
# One rule per line:  <kind> <name> <rest of the line>
# Comment lines start with `#`; there are no trailing comments. Patterns are POSIX extended regular
# expressions (bash `[[ =~ ]]`) matched against a repository-relative path. Several lines of one
# kind and name are alternatives.
#
#   everything -  <re>   a change to this path turns every CI job on
#   job <job>     <re>   a change to this path can affect the CI job (ci.yml `changes` output)
#   except <job>  <re>   ... unless it also matches this (a path that cannot affect the job)
#   keep <job>    <re>   ... except that a path matching this stays a trigger after all
#   gate <gate>   <re>   a change to this path turns the preflight gate on (gates that have no CI job)
#   lane <job> <needs> <command...>   how hack/lane-gates.sh runs the local gate of a CI job:
#                        <needs> is a comma list of tools (docker,helm,go) or `-`; <command> is
#                        `preflight` (the preflight gate of the same name) or a make target line
#   script-check - <cmd> a static check or script test of the quick checks, lint-shell and scripts
#                        CI jobs that takes seconds: the preflight gate `scripts` runs it. @BASE@
#                        is the merge base with the preflight base, @HEAD@ is HEAD
#   script-skip -  <cmd> a script step of those jobs that preflight does not run (slow, covered by
#                        another gate, or not runnable on a Mac); hack/paths-test.sh fails when a
#                        step of ci.yml is in neither list
#   e2e-binary -  <pkg>  a command test/e2e/run.sh builds and loads into kind
#   e2e-needed -  <re>   needs the kind e2e (hack/needs-e2e.sh)
#   e2e-forced -  <re>   needs the kind e2e, even if e2e-ignored matches (the e2e's own files)
#   e2e-ignored - <re>   does not need it, unless forced or in a binary's build graph
#
# FAIL CLOSED: a path that no rule mentions runs the job. `job go .` below is that catch-all for
# the Go jobs; `except go` lists what cannot affect them. To skip a job for a path, name the path
# in an `except` rule and say why in the comment above it.

# --- Changes that run everything: CI itself, the Makefile, the Go module, and these rules ---------
# `everything ci` is CI plumbing: the workflow and the scripts that decide what it runs. `everything -` is the
# build inputs. Both turn everything on; hack/pr-merge.sh --admin asks hack/ci-changes.sh to ignore the plumbing
# rule (CI_CHANGES_IGNORE_PLUMBING=1) when it decides whether `flavors` is owed, because a plumbing change by itself
# cannot get a branch `flavors` run and `--admin` is the only route of a `.github/**` pull request.
everything ci ^(\.github/workflows/ci\.yml|\.github/actions/setup-go-cache/action\.yml|hack/ci-changes\.sh|hack/ci-skip-heavy\.sh|hack/paths\.rules|hack/paths-lib\.sh)$
everything - ^(Makefile|go\.mod|go\.sum)$

# --- go: go-tidy, go-lint, go-test (Postgres), go-race --------------------------------------------
# Any path can affect them, except what is listed here. Not listed on purpose: charts/, test/,
# internal/, cmd/ (Go tests read them), hack/versions.env and hack/dev/ (Go tests read them), and
# every non-Go file under hack/ outside the directories and files excepted below.
job go .
# Documentation, the web app (own jobs; its Go files stay a trigger by `keep`), and GitHub's
# non-CI files (other workflows and actions are separate jobs; ci.yml itself is `everything`).
except go \.md$
except go ^docs/
except go ^web/
except go ^\.github/
except go ^\.claude/
# Top-level shell scripts of hack/, hook scripts and chart assertions: the Go jobs run Go, and the
# few scripts they call are listed in `keep`. The script tests run in the `scripts` job.
except go ^hack/[^/]+\.sh$
except go ^hack/hooks/
# The failure-class table and its log samples are read only by hack/ci-fail.sh and its test, and the
# recorded records of hack/ci-timing.sh only by its test; they run in the `scripts` job, no Go job reads them.
except go ^hack/ci-fail-classes\.tsv$
except go ^hack/testdata/ci-fail/
except go ^hack/testdata/ci-timing/
except go ^hack/chart-check\.d/
# The scripts the Go jobs run or the Go tests execute: go-test.sh and what it starts, the lint
# wrapper, the agentgateway pin (go-test pulls the image), the compat fixture recorder
# (internal/compat) and harness-tag.sh (test/harnesses).
keep go ^hack/(go-test|go-test-host|golangci-lint|agentgateway-pin|record-compat-fixtures|harness-tag)\.sh$
keep go \.go$

# --- tidy: go-tidy and go-lint (#572) ----------------------------------------------------------------
# `go mod tidy` and golangci-lint read Go sources and the module files, nothing else (the lint
# configuration is an input of go-lint only, but costs go-tidy a minute at most), so both run when a
# .go file, go.mod/go.sum or the lint configuration changes. go-test and go-race stay under
# `job go`, which any file can turn on. A change to ci.yml, the Makefile or these rules runs them
# through `everything`. The preflight gate `tidy` uses the same rules.
job tidy \.go$
job tidy ^go\.(mod|sum)$
job tidy ^\.golangci\.ya?ml$

# --- vuln: go-vuln, govulncheck on a change of the Go dependencies (#579 part 2) --------------------------
# A change of the module's requirements (go.mod, go.sum) can bring in a reachable known vulnerability, so
# a pull request that changes them runs govulncheck. New reachability from a code change (a .go change that
# starts to call a vulnerable symbol of a module already required, or of the standard library) and a new
# advisory are caught by the nightly run, up to one day later. The rules are explicit although `everything`
# also turns every job on for go.mod and go.sum: hack/paths-test.sh checks the rule itself, so narrowing it
# is seen. The nested modules of hack/spike/ are deliberately not scanned (the anchors keep them out).
# A change of the check itself runs it: the script, the nightly workflow and the tool pin. hack/versions.env
# is a path of many pull requests (every tool bump); that cost is accepted, one govulncheck run of about a
# minute. A change to ci.yml, the Makefile, the setup-go-cache action or these rules runs it through
# `everything`. The preflight gate `vuln` uses the same rules.
job vuln ^go\.(mod|sum)$
job vuln ^hack/govulncheck\.sh$
job vuln ^\.github/workflows/govulncheck\.yml$
job vuln ^hack/versions\.env$

# --- shell: lint-shell (#572) --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# shellcheck over `git ls-files '*.sh'` (any directory), and actionlint and zizmor over .github/ (workflows,
# the composite actions they read, their config). The tool versions and checksums are in hack/versions.env,
# read through hack/versions-env.sh.
job shell \.sh$
job shell ^\.github/
job shell ^\.shellcheckrc$
job shell ^hack/versions(-env\.sh|\.env)$

# --- scripts: the `scripts` CI job and the preflight gate of that name (#572) -------------------------
# The job runs about 65 script tests and static checks. They read the tracked shell scripts,
# workflows, Dockerfiles, Go sources (mktemp, audit and bash5 lints, the `go list` graphs of
# needs-e2e), web/package.json and the lockfile (e2e-remote-test), the flavors, test/e2e and
# CONTRIBUTING.md (versions-check), docs/dev/ci.md (ci-cache-test) and docs/adr (adr-lint tests), measured
# 2026-11-11 by deleting each directory and running the job's steps. So the job fails closed like
# `job go`: it runs for every path except the ones below. The one check that reads every file of the
# tree, hack/old-issue-refs-lint.sh, is a step of `quick checks`, which always runs.
job scripts .
# Markdown and docs the script checks do not read; web/src is TypeScript only (its Go stubs and
# package.json stay triggers).
except scripts \.md$
except scripts ^docs/
except scripts ^web/src/
keep scripts ^(AGENTS|CONTRIBUTING)\.md$
keep scripts ^docs/(adr/|metadata/|dev/ci\.md$)
keep scripts \.go$

# --- web ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
job web ^(web/|api/proto/)

# --- generate: every input and output of `make generate` ------------------------------------------
# hack/ci-changes-test.sh derives them from the Makefile and the generator configs and fails when
# one is missing here: the protos and the vendored OpenShell and agentgateway protos, the OpenAPI
# spec and its config, the sqlc inputs, the buf and sqlc configs, protoc-gen-es (web/package.json,
# its lockfile) and the outputs.
# hack/generate.sh is the body of `make generate` (#349): a wrapper-only edit must still run the job.
job generate ^(api/proto/|third_party/openshell/proto/|third_party/agentgateway/proto/|api/admin/v1/(openapi|oapi-codegen)\.yaml$|internal/adminapi/api\.gen\.go$|internal/db/(queries|migrations|store)/|internal/audit/internal/auditstore/|sqlc\.yaml|buf\.|internal/gen/|web/src/gen/|docs/reference/proto/|cmd/protoc-gen-koinon-doc/|web/package\.json$|web/pnpm-lock\.yaml$|hack/generate\.sh$)

# --- chart: chart-check.sh sources hack/versions.env and every hack/chart-check.d/*.sh -----------
job chart ^(charts/|hack/chart-check\.sh|hack/chart-check\.d/|hack/chartlint/|hack/versions\.env$)

# --- chartsmoke: the chart's Jobs and Deployments run as containers (up to 35 minutes) ------------
# The suite renders the chart and builds each cmd/koinon-* binary with `go build ./cmd/<name>` and
# no build tags (test/chartsmoke/images_test.go). Go packages those commands and the suite import
# (and files they embed) are derived by hack/ci-changes.sh (`go list`, like flavors). This seed
# covers what the graph cannot name: the chart itself, hack/versions.env (tool pins the job and
# the suite's helpers read), the suite's own tree, and go.mod/go.sum.
job chartsmoke ^(charts/|test/chartsmoke/|hack/versions\.env$|go\.(mod|sum))
# The go-list graph's package directory `web` would also match web/src and package.json; the suite
# builds without the `webui` tag, so only the Go stubs under web/ can change a binary.
except chartsmoke ^web/
# keep wins over except (#524 Bugbot): must not reinclude web/*_test.go (ERE, no lookaround).
keep chartsmoke ^web/(.*/)?([^/]*[^t]|[^/]*[^s]t|[^/]*[^e]st|[^/]*[^t]est|[^/]*[^_]test|[^/]{1,4})\.go$
# Test files of other packages are not compiled into a binary or into the suite's imports; the
# suite's own _test.go files are under test/chartsmoke/ (seed) and stay.
except chartsmoke ^(cmd|internal|connectors|api|pricing|web)/.*_test\.go$

# --- escape: the admission specs (the only ones CI runs) read the chart and the testenv helper -----
# The reconciler-side cases need kind or the lab (#66), so their packages are not triggers.
job escape ^(charts/|test/escape/|internal/testing/testenv/)

# --- flavors: the suite's Go imports are added by hack/ci-changes.sh (go list graph) ----------------
job flavors ^(harnesses/|internal/(agentd|harness|acp)/|test/harnesses/|hack/harness-tag\.sh|hack/probe-tag\.sh|hack/spike/probe/|templates/)

# --- opencodeplugin: tsc and node --test of Koinon's OpenCode plugins' CI-only dev project ----------
# (ADR 0093 decision 4). A change under harnesses/opencode/plugins/ also matches `job flavors` above
# (the Dockerfile COPYs the plugin module, and test/harnesses proves it loads), so both jobs run; this
# one is the fast, Docker-free type-check and unit-test pass. The Dockerfile is a trigger too: the job
# checks that the types pin equals the image's OpenCode pin, so a re-pin type-checks against new types.
job opencodeplugin ^harnesses/opencode/(plugins/|Dockerfile$)

# --- local gates of the CI jobs (hack/lane-gates.sh) -------------------------------------------------
# A job without a lane line has no local gate and is reported as not run.
lane go - preflight
lane web - preflight
lane generate - preflight
lane chart - preflight
lane chartsmoke docker,helm,go test-chart-smoke
# hack/harness-repro-check.sh (two uncached builds, one digest) is the advisory workflow flavor-repro.yml, not a ci.yml job; it has no lane.
lane flavors docker,go test-harnesses
lane opencodeplugin pnpm test-opencode-plugin
lane escape helm,go test-admission
lane tidy - preflight
lane vuln - preflight
lane shell - preflight
lane scripts - preflight

# --- preflight gates that have no CI job of their own ------------------------------------------------
# (go, generate, chart, web, tidy and scripts use the `job` rules above, so preflight and CI agree.)
gate go \.go$
gate deps (^|/)(go\.mod|go\.sum|package\.json|pnpm-lock\.yaml|package-lock\.json|yarn\.lock|Dockerfile[^/]*)$
gate proto \.proto$
gate migrate ^internal/db/migrations/
gate adr ^(docs/(adr|research|spikes|metadata)/|hack/(adr-|doc-meta-))
gate shell \.sh$
gate actionlint ^\.github/(workflows/[^/]*\.ya?ml|actionlint\.ya?ml)$
gate zizmor ^\.github/(workflows/[^/]*\.ya?ml|actions/.*\.ya?ml|zizmor\.ya?ml|dependabot\.ya?ml)$
gate runnerlint ^(\.github/(workflows/[^/]*\.ya?ml|actionlint\.ya?ml)|hack/runner-lint[^/]*\.sh)$
gate pinned \.sh$
gate pinned ^\.github/workflows/[^/]*\.yml$
gate pinned ^\.github/actions/
gate mktemp \.sh$
gate mktemp ^Makefile$
gate mktemp ^\.github/workflows/[^/]*\.yml$
gate mktemp ^internal/.*\.go$
gate bash5 \.sh$
gate audit \.go$
gate audit ^internal/db/queries/.*\.sql$
gate audit ^hack/audit-batch-lint
gate versions ^(hack/versions|hack/e2e-toolchain/|CONTRIBUTING\.md$|\.github/workflows/[^/]*\.yml$|hack/chart-check\.sh$|hack/[^/]*\.sh$|test/e2e/.*\.sh$)
# --- script checks: what `preflight` runs of the `quick checks`, `lint-shell` and `scripts` jobs -------
# Checks that take seconds (measured 2026-11-09 on a Mac: at most 15 s each). The gates adr,
# migrate, mktemp, pinned, bash5, audit, versions, shell, actionlint and zizmor run their own.
script-check - hack/migrate-lint-test.sh
script-check - hack/migrate-renumber-test.sh
script-check - hack/commit-subject-check-test.sh
script-check - hack/commit-subject-check.sh @BASE@ HEAD
script-check - hack/git-identity-check-test.sh
script-check - hack/git-identity-check.sh range @BASE@ HEAD
script-check - hack/koinon-fetch-test.sh
script-check - hack/fetch-pinned-test.sh
script-check - hack/e2e-parts-test.sh
script-check - hack/apt-retries-test.sh --self-test
script-check - hack/apt-retries-test.sh
script-check - hack/e2e-remote-test.sh
script-check - hack/ci-fail-test.sh
script-check - hack/ci-timing-test.sh
script-check - hack/ci-go-gate-test.sh
script-check - hack/ci-web-gate-test.sh
script-check - hack/govulncheck-test.sh
script-check - hack/ci-required-test.sh
script-check - hack/repo-contract-test.sh
script-check - hack/tmp-safety-test.sh
script-check - hack/notes-expiry-test.sh
script-check - hack/old-issue-refs-lint-test.sh
script-check - hack/old-issue-refs-lint.sh
script-check - hack/agentgateway-pin-test.sh
script-check - hack/agentgateway-pin.sh --check
script-check - hack/golangci-lint-test.sh
script-check - hack/preflight-stop-test.sh
script-check - hack/e2e-decide-test.sh
script-check - hack/kind-registry-test.sh
script-check - hack/drill-issue-test.sh
script-check - hack/hooks/agent-spawn-check_test.sh
script-check - hack/hooks/read-hooks_test.sh
script-check - hack/agent-state-test.sh
script-check - hack/dep-age-check-test.sh
script-check - hack/ubuntu-snapshot-bump_test.sh
script-check - hack/buf-breaking-against-test.sh
script-check - hack/lane-gates-test.sh
script-check - hack/generate-test.sh
script-check - hack/ci-supersede-test.sh
script-check - hack/ci-concurrency-test.sh
script-check - hack/ci-merge-group-test.sh
script-check - hack/secrets-skip-test.sh
script-check - hack/route-guard-test.sh
script-check - hack/ci-cache-test.sh
script-check - hack/ci-rules-check-test.sh
script-check - hack/ci-rules-check.sh
script-check - hack/e2e-commands-check.sh
script-check - hack/chart-check-test.sh
script-check - hack/paths-test.sh
script-check - hack/runner-lint-test.sh
script-check - hack/runner-lint.sh
script-check - hack/go-test-host-test.sh
script-check - hack/ci-playwright-image-test.sh
# Slow (23 to 85 s; CI runs them): the decision rule's own tests need
# `go list`, the others start many git repositories.
script-skip - hack/needs-e2e-test.sh
script-skip - hack/ci-changes-test.sh
script-skip - hack/versions-check-test.sh
script-skip - hack/pr-wait-test.sh
script-skip - hack/pr-merge-test.sh
script-skip - hack/go-test-test.sh
script-skip - hack/ship-test.sh
script-skip - hack/preflight-test.sh
script-skip - hack/release-gate-test.sh
script-skip - hack/ci-skip-heavy-test.sh
script-skip - hack/claim_test.sh
script-skip - hack/migrate-lint.sh
# Needs a UTF-8 locale with its own collation: CI generates en_US.UTF-8 in a separate step first.
script-skip - hack/harness-tag-test.sh
script-skip - hack/flavor-tag-test.sh # the earlier name, an alias link ci.yml still calls (#610)
# Fail on a Mac with the sandbox's /private/tmp paths or its git setup; they run on Linux in CI.
script-skip - hack/wt-test.sh
script-skip - hack/wt-install-test.sh
script-skip - hack/e2e-bisect-test.sh
# Covered by another preflight gate (versions, mktemp, pinned, bash5, audit, adr).
script-skip - hack/versions-check.sh
script-skip - hack/mktemp-lint-test.sh
script-skip - hack/mktemp-lint.sh
script-skip - hack/pinned-download-lint.sh
script-skip - hack/audit-batch-lint-test.sh
script-skip - hack/audit-batch-lint.sh
script-skip - hack/bash5-lint-test.sh
script-skip - hack/bash5-lint.sh
script-skip - hack/adr-lint-test.sh
script-skip - hack/adr-lint.sh
script-skip - hack/doc-meta-lint-test.sh
script-skip - hack/doc-meta-lint.sh

# --- the kind e2e (hack/needs-e2e.sh) ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Needed for changes whose behaviour only a full install observes: startup, flags and environment,
# chart objects including Jobs, the schema, cross-service flows, the harness, and the e2e itself
# (old issue 281 changed branch naming in githubtools; old issue 284 a startup flag the chart's
# migrate Job lacked). Unit and package tests cannot see those.
#
# Go code is not listed by directory: the binaries are the commands test/e2e/kind/images.sh (run.sh and the drill) builds with ko
# (the three services and the three fakes it deploys; hack/needs-e2e-test.sh checks them against
# its `ko build` line). A non-test file in the directory of a package in their dependency graph
# (`go list -deps`, this module only), or below it (embedded files), is relevant.
e2e-binary - ./cmd/koinon-api
e2e-binary - ./cmd/koinon-reconciler
e2e-binary - ./cmd/koinon-agentd
e2e-binary - ./cmd/koinon-fakemodel
e2e-binary - ./cmd/koinon-fakegithub
e2e-binary - ./cmd/koinon-fakemcp
#
# A path is relevant when it is forced, or needed and not ignored, or in the build graph.
# Needed. A renamed binary directory breaks `go list` (that also fails closed), so cmd/ is a backstop.
e2e-needed - ^cmd/
e2e-needed - ^vendor/
e2e-needed - ^charts/
e2e-needed - ^internal/db/migrations/
e2e-needed - ^harnesses/
# Dependency changes reach the binaries.
e2e-needed - ^go\.(mod|sum)$
e2e-needed - ^go\.work(\.sum)?$
# test-e2e-kind is `make test-e2e-kind`.
e2e-needed - ^Makefile$
# How ko builds the six images.
e2e-needed - ^\.ko\.yaml$
# The chart's image pins, if present.
e2e-needed - ^release/versions\.yaml$
# Forced: the e2e runs the quickstart's shell blocks, so the quickstart page is an input although it
# is Markdown, and the e2e's own test files are the e2e, not "Go tests outside it".
# The driver, run.sh, kind/ (up.sh, fakes, values).
e2e-forced - ^test/e2e/
# run.sh calls test/escape/kind.sh through test/e2e/escape-openshell.sh and escape-mcp.sh.
e2e-forced - ^test/escape/
# The probe image kind.sh pulls or builds, and the tag it is pulled under (#482).
e2e-forced - ^hack/(spike/probe/|probe-tag\.sh$)
e2e-forced - ^\.github/workflows/e2e-kind\.yml$
# Agent prompts and instructions may be Markdown.
e2e-forced - ^harnesses/.*\.md$
# run.sh runs the quickstart blocks (test/e2e/commands/*.e1) through docs-e1.sh, names the flavor image with harness-tag.sh
# and sets its base image with harness-base.sh (HARNESS_BASE, #200).
e2e-forced - ^hack/docs-e1\.sh$
e2e-forced - ^hack/harness-tag\.sh$
e2e-forced - ^hack/harness-base\.sh$
# The earlier names, alias links the workflows still call until they use the new names (#610).
e2e-forced - ^hack/flavor-(tag|base)\.sh$
# The kind, ko and helm versions e2e-kind.yml installs (old issue 565), the filter that loads them
# into the workflow's environment, and the downloader it uses (#431).
e2e-forced - ^hack/versions\.env$
e2e-forced - ^hack/versions-env\.sh$
e2e-forced - ^hack/fetch-pinned\.sh$
# The web toolchain image run.sh uses (Chromium for the browser suite).
e2e-forced - ^hack/e2e-toolchain/
# Not needed (unless forced). Playwright covers the web app; hack/ holds scripts the e2e does not
# call (see forced); Go tests outside test/e2e are not the e2e.
e2e-ignored - \.md$
e2e-ignored - ^docs/
e2e-ignored - ^web/
e2e-ignored - ^hack/
e2e-ignored - /testdata/
e2e-ignored - _test\.go$
